6. RESEARCH USE AND VALIDATION

The Software provides computational tools for protein preparation, water
sampling, molecular dynamics, hydration-site clustering, thermodynamic
analysis, hydrogen-bond analysis, ligand displacement scoring, and associated
visualization and data processing. It is supplied as a research tool without
representing that its algorithms or outputs have been validated for a
particular protein, ligand, molecular complex, biological target, assay,
experimental condition, or downstream application.

You are responsible for deciding whether the Software is appropriate for
your intended use and independently checking the scientific correctness of
its inputs, methods, assumptions, parameters, and outputs. Relevant checks
include structural preparation, atom and residue identities, biological
assembly, missing atoms or residues, protonation and terminal states,
cofactors, binding-site definitions, force fields, water models, calibration
references, sampling, convergence, coordinate frames, and units.

Before relying on results for synthesis, experimental work, drug discovery,
drug development, or manufacturing, arrange verification and validation
appropriate to that use, qualified professional review, and compliance with
applicable laws and institutional requirements. A computed hydration site,
energy, entropy estimate, or displacement score does not by itself establish
binding affinity, kinetic behavior, chemical validity, biological activity,
protein function or stability, safety, toxicity, efficacy, or manufacturability.

Permission to use the Software, including commercial permission, does not
constitute the licensor's validation, recommendation, or approval of an
experiment, compound, product, or application. Maintenance, technical support,
correction of errors, and future releases are not promised. These conditions
allocate responsibility; they do not certify results or substitute for
appropriate experimental validation and safeguards.

